    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW21jZfxe5AmskoMP3AYBnVbr)_\n\nFollow-up to #31, whose splash looked unchanged on Sia's machine.\n\nBefore: `M-x sp-splash-screen` only switched to an existing `*splash*` buffer, so the new art never appeared until that buffer was killed. When the art was drawn, every other character was dropped, because `sp-splash--put-art-char` skipped a character when the line already ended at its column.\n\nAfter: called interactively, `sp-splash-screen` kills an old `*splash*` first and redraws. The art is complete, and the dark/light greys are a little stronger (`#454b5c` / `#cfd3dc`). `sp-splash.org` is updated in step, with a CHANGELOG entry.\n\nHow it was checked: in headless Emacs 29.3 (stubbing `nerd-icons-faicon`, 120x50 frame) the splash shows the full lambda behind Agenda/Config/Mail/Notes/Projects with the text on top, and `sp-splash-art-right` moves it and redraws. The doc's blocks tangle to the same text as the `.el`.\n\nNot checked: colours and layout in a real GUI frame with the PNG-capable build, and your themes.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01T2BcMQ3qdNUiW5oZRLQRsG)_",
